# Rule: Scroll animations & cockpit hooks

Shared scroll progress, cockpit integration, and home-v2 corridor-exit compositing. Changes affect Lenis, GSAP, HUD behavior, and the corridor→Services seam.

**Read first:** `sentinel/decisions/002-scroll-animation-architecture.md`, `sentinel/decisions/005-scroll-captured-content-reveal.md`, `sentinel/decisions/018-home-v2-depth-corridor.md`, `sentinel/decisions/021-corridor-exit-zoom-dissipate.md`.

**Process:** `sentinel/MAINTENANCE.md` - document contract changes with an ADR or decision addendum.

**Home-v2 corridor-exit invariant (ADR-021, 2026-06-19 amendment):** the production seam after the corridor epilogue is a **short zoom-dissipate** that resolves as `#services` (now a content section — terminal Keynote/Workshop/Embedded cards mounted via `ServicesPortal`) reaches the viewport top. `useCorridorExitScroll` owns the dissipate clock: `DISSIPATE_SCROLL_SPAN_VH = 0.9` (was 2.0), eased through `corridorExitSpeedRamp` (smootherstep) into `--corridor-dissipate` / `dockProgress`. The hook also writes `data-corridor-docked` (fixed canvas promotion), `data-corridor-exit` + `--corridor-exit-veil` (body veil capped at `VEIL_DOCK_CAP = 0.55`, clears when dock releases). The brandmark fades out with the dissipating sphere across `DISSIPATE_FADE_START 0.5 → DISSIPATE_FADE_END 0.95` of the smoothed dock clock (applied in `ProjectedBrandmarkActor`'s tracker `onPaint` and the post-active rAF) — NO in-section re-centre, hold, pixel-field, or ambient haze. Keep the dock channel (`docked` / `dockProgress`) writes scoped to one hook; do not write `epilogueProgress` / `paintProgress` from the exit hook. The retired cover-plane sweep recipe (lower opaque plane covers a held canvas, first-read copy lives inside the cover) is preserved in `components/landing/home-v2/handoff-lab/` + `/test/handoff-a|b|c` and documented in ADR-021 — reuse that recipe verbatim if a later section needs an Active Theory / Hashgraph-class cover sweep; do not rebuild it.

**Retired in-#services brandmark beats (ADR-021 2026-06-19 amendment — do NOT reintroduce without an ADR amendment):** the four follow-up choreography phases that once owned `#services` are retired in favour of an opaque content section: (1) **welded re-centre lerp** in `ProjectedBrandmarkActor` (`DOCK_RECENTRE_FRAC` + the welded → viewport-centre lerp + `getServicesTargetHalfPx` local helper); (2) **`data-services-brandmark`** actor-lifecycle gate (`"hold"` / `"fade"`) + `--services-brandmark` opacity var + the continuum-approach fade; (3) **`data-services-pixelate`** + `--services-pixelate` + `transform.seamMorph` + the `CorridorSeamPixelField` 2D canvas mount; (4) **`data-services-ambient`** + `--services-ambient` + `transform.servicesAmbient` / `servicesAmbientLevel` + the R3F painter ambient branches (`FlyingCameraRig` dockHeld, `MotionFollowerDriver` pinned dissipate, `ShellSubstrateGyro` interior cloud composition, `StaticStarfield` ambient-scaled boost, `BrandmarkPhysicsCoreActor` handoffFade=0). The supporting pure helpers (`servicesAmbientOpacityMultiplier`, `SERVICES_AMBIENT_HOLD_LEVEL`, `lib/home-v2/seamPixelize.ts`, `getServicesTargetHalfPx` canonical export) stay in the tree as reusable reference material; the store still carries `seamMorph` / `servicesAmbient` / `servicesAmbientLevel` for source-compat but `useCorridorExitScroll` writes them as `0` / `false` / `0` permanently. The painter ambient branches no-op cleanly when the flag is false; the `useDepthScroll` reverse-scroll release for `servicesAmbient` stays as a defensive no-op. If a future section needs any of these recipes, port them verbatim from this ADR's history — do not rebuild from scratch.

**Hero → Thoughtform seam invariant (ADR-022 v8):** the hero → corridor seam is a **ToyFight curtain reveal** — the **hero is the moving layer** (`.hero`, `position: relative; z-index: 4`) that scrolls up and off the first viewport, uncovering the corridor's parked `ThoughtformCompassGate` frame held **frozen** behind it (`.home-corridor-host` z:3). NOT the inverse (v7's mistake: a held hero with the corridor rising to cover it), and NEVER a proxy/copy of the second section (v6's mistake). The freeze: `useLandingScroll` toggles `html[data-corridor-entry]` while the corridor stage top is below the viewport top, and `home-v2.css` makes `.home-v2-stage__sticky` `position: fixed; inset: 0` under that flag. At the handoff the flag clears and native sticky resumes at the same `top: 0`, with no transform on the sticky cell and never on `.home-v2-stage`. The hero may receive only a tiny capped inertial `translateY` correction for ToyFight-like smoothness; document scroll, corridor `progress` / `paintProgress` / `epilogueProgress` / `dockProgress`, and the hero video opacity remain untouched. Hero video stays opaque, never scaled/faded (ADR-008 Rule 3, gateway shield). ADR-022 history documents every superseded approach (v6 proxy sweep, v7 held-hero parallax/counter-translate) and its artifact.
